@page "/privacy"
@model Site.Pages.PrivacyModel
<div class="container narrow">
    <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
    <p class="muted">Last updated: October 2026</p>

    <h2>What this site is</h2>
    <p>
        Document Number Validator is a documentation and demo site for an open-source .NET library.
        It is built to work without tracking.
    </p>

    <h2>Cookies and analytics</h2>
    <p>
        This site does not use advertising or analytics cookies and does not include third-party trackers.
        The only browser storage used is your colour-theme preference (<code>localStorage</code>), which never
        leaves your device.
    </p>

    <h2>Demo inputs</h2>
    <p>
        Values you enter in the on-page demo are processed in memory on the server for the current request
        so that validation can run. They are not persisted, logged to the application data store or shared
        with third parties. Do not enter real personal or financial data into the demo.
    </p>

    <h2>Server logs</h2>
    <p>
        As with any hosted website, the hosting provider may keep standard infrastructure logs (such as IP
        address, requested URL and timestamp) for security and operations purposes.
    </p>

    <h2>Open source</h2>
    <p>
        The website source and the validator libraries are public on
        <a href="@SiteInfo.WebsiteRepositoryUrl" rel="noopener">GitHub</a>. If you have questions or want to
        request a change, open an issue.
    </p>
</div>
